  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Priority Outcome 1: Improved Basic Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kiribati Education Improvement Program (KEIP) is the framework through which Australia supports the implementation of the Ministry of Education&#x2019;s Education Sector Strategic Plan and its goal of improving the quality of education provided in schools in Kiribati.
KEIP Phase I (2011-2012) supported the Ministry of Education to establish the enabling environment for subsequent phases of KEIP. Phase II (2013-2015) focused on improving teaching and learning outcomes in years 1-4. 
KEIP current Phase III (2016-2020) valued at $38 million seeks to embed previous reforms and extend the reforms to upper primary school (years 5-6) and into junior secondary schools, focusing on two end of program outcomes improving learning outcomes for basic education for girls and boys, including children with a disability by improving : curriculum in the upper primary (Year 5-6) and JSS curriculum; learning environments; quality teaching and school leadership; inclusive education and sector management.</narrative>
  </description>
